WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.920
Wren: So, we took that 3D model that Sam had downloaded and augmented.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.740
You can see here it's like it's got these weird fracture points like, like break this.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.920
It's actually already broken.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.780
We also have the GoPro Session.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.220
You can put it here in the middle.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.660
The issue is that this is so low down that it's like all the GoPro's are all gonna be in the shot.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.500
Just modeled a quick little thing here.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.680
Basically put the little GoPro here in
that and this will sit in the rig here.

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:28.680
It's weird that there aren't really any
dimensions for the session online.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.920
But I just- I literally just want to know

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:31.820
how thick it was

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:32.860
how long it was

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.100
how wide it was.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.240
I measured it myself.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.320
It is not 35 millimeters it is 38 millimeters.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.240
Cmike: Hey Jake.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.200
Jake: Oh hey.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.000
Alright, so what do you need to make a Metal Gear Solid Bionic Arm?

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.730
Well, first things first, you need an
under-layer.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.490
One left-handed black glove.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.480
One left sleeve of a black shirt.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.200
Crafting foam; You can buy this online
but it's basically like yoga foam.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.740
Outside of a Clorox disinfecting wipes can.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.100
You know, materials should come cheap.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.960
Heat gun; use with adult supervision or...

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.040
you know what to do.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.620
Is it latex paint?

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.660
Let's see what happens.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.960
It's just like kindergarten.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.880
You know, I was telling Wren earlier,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.240
Wren might be the engineer who became a VFX artist and creator,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.780
and I'm the lawyer who became a prop maker.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.800
And that's what you need,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.000
you start from there.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.820
Wren: Sent this over to Spencer over in Stress Level Zero

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.420
To print it on their 3D printer.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.160
So let's go check out if it turned out well.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.460
Wren: Wait, do you have records to play on it?

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.220
Sam: I got like one.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:40.920
Wren: That's enough.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:41.660
Sam: Ha, yep.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.160
Wren: Haha.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.080
There's the guy I wanted to see.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.320
Spencer: You've been looking for me?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.220
Wren: Do you know if the print turned out well?

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:49.720
Spencer: Yes.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:50.220
Wren: It did?

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:50.720
Spencer: Yes.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.780
Wren: *excited clap* Let's go check it out!

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.100
There it is!

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.540
Makerbot Replicator 2X.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.400
Wren: Shall we?

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.020
Spencer: You shall.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.340
Wren: Moment of truth.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.480
It is...ok I don't want to break it.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.140
So, hopefully this will fit.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.060
*gasp* it does!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.040
A little tighter next time, maybe. *Ba-dum-tss*

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.440
Now for the second moment of truth, if you don't mind holding this.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.300
I brought the session!

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.020
*drumroll*

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.700
Nooooooooo!

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.260
We reprinted this piece.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.460
One percent bigger.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.800
It finally fits now

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.120
and it's way tighter in the hole.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.720
It goes all the way down so it's like we
have all the angles looking outwards.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.660
The only piece you're missing from a rig like this is
literally just the bottom patch.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.920
In effects, you can literally go in and like throw a
tile down at the bottom.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.860
Now this rig is entirely finished and in fact we could probably actually use this for the final thing.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:45.360
Well, it wiggles a bit, but I mean it's not gonna be moving so it's not a big deal.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.480
Niko: Amazon! Our favorite retailer!

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.400
Wait, are these the cool chairs or are these the dumb chairs?

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.040
Cmike: These are the same chairs that we all are getting.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:53.680
Niko: Those ones?

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.180
Cmike: Yeah.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.840
Niko: Oh, well I got a special chair for myself.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.260
So, we're gonna have three nice chairs?

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.340
*Niko mumbling*

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:02.740
Sam: Get down!

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.240
Huh

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.280
Sam: Oh, what?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.620
Hehe it bounced off the handle.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.120
Niko: Can you give me the Arnold Schwarzenegger quote one more time?

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.200
Sam: Get this Choppa off of me!

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.680
Niko: Take that!!

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.420
What uuupp?!

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.120
I did it!

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.260
Sam: Screw that wall!

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.500
*misses*

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.960
*mumbling* I hate knives.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:23.720
*sticks the landing*

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.400
All: OOOOHHHHH!

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.360
Niko: I love knives!

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.800
*laughter*

